    "raw": "Grooming backlog for the todo.py / todo_web.py tooling (repo: jovlinger/utils,\nskills/projectmanagement/todos). Captured as pre-init; needs grooming/breakdown\nbefore work. Items below are the raw requirements as stated.\n\n1. Rename states (nouns, not gerunds). Rename pre-init (current state key `pre`)\n   -> GROOM, and `init` -> READY. Other states are fine as-is. Update the skill\n   references / SKILL.md too, not just the code. (VALID_STATES in todo.py already\n   carries a \"# rename to ready\" note on `init`.) General principle: prefer nouns\n   over gerunds for state names.\n\n2. Search weighting. When the query includes a field-scoped term like `todo:xxx`\n   or `sha:xxx`, weight matches on those fields very highly. Still run the vector\n   search as well -- the field-scoped boost is on top of vector recall, not\n   instead of it.\n\n3. State-match search terms. Support `state:` search terms using the existing\n   filter grammar (see STATE_SET_ALIASES / parse_state_filter: `+` = union,\n   `-` = difference, `,` = `+`). Single states like `state:ready`, expressions\n   with a shared prefix like `state:ready+wait`, and named groups like\n   `state:active` and `state:workable-groom`. NOTE: there may already be a todo\n   about this -- check and dedupe/link before implementing.\n\n4. Priority: add a new priority field on the todo.\n\n5. Sort terms. For some fields, support special search terms `desc` / `asc` to\n   sort results by that field.\n\n6. Search-box value model. The search box holds space-separated values of two\n   kinds: (a) free text -- any token NOT matching `key:val` syntax -- which is\n   equivalent to `text:\"...\"`; and (b) `key:val` terms, some of which have\n   special handling (e.g. sorting). A `key:val` whose key is not recognized is\n   text-ified (folded back into the free-text search).\n\n7. Web tab title. The browser tab title should always be `todo web:<port>`\n   regardless of what is currently being viewed."
  },
